                <pb facs="0145" n="111" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg111"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 75.</note>
                <head>Mr. E. B. Washburne to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[By cable telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1870-09-05"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 5, 1870</date>.
                        (Received September 5.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fish,</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Washington:</hi></p>
                <p>Republic proclaimed. Government of national defense announced this morning
                    composed of deputies of Paris. Favre, minister of foreign affairs; Gambetta,
                    interior; Picard, finance; Simon, public instruction; Cremieux, justice;
                    Kératry, prefect of police; Arago, prefect of Seine; Glais-Bizon, director of
                    telegraphs; Trochu, governor of Paris and minister of war. Paris quiet. Instruct
                    me.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WASHBURNE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
